          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: استجاب",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "استجاب — istajāba — \"to respond\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "استجاب المدير لطلب العمال. istajāba al-mudīr li-ṭalab al-ʿummāl. The manager responded to the workers' request."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Present: يستجيب, yastajīb."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It takes لـ: استجاب (istajāba) لـ …."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "استجاب (istajāba) is built on the native Arabic root j-w-b, \"to cut through; to answer\" (Lane). It is Form X, to give the answer sought: to respond. جواب, an answer, is from the same root."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
